  "behavior": [
    "Runtime.PublishObservations validates and retains original caller-supplied observations through runtime ownership and the catalog input transaction. It reads no source.",
    "Distinct concurrent manual calls serialize without coalescing. Observations already in manual history do not advance the sequence or broadcast another generation.",
    "Aggregate provider observations retain their original provider set, payload checksum, and safe receipt. Diagnostic messages are absent from retained records.",
    "Provider history preserves earlier facts through later omissions. Shared reconciliation orders fallback before direct evidence and then observation time. Equal-priority conflicts require corrected input.",
    "Separate metadata passes preserve multiple reviewed inputs from the same source within one atomic publication.",
    "Restart excludes inactive bindings and rejects changed selectors without a new revision. Rejected and canceled input cannot change accepted history.",
    "Recovery validates the entire parent history before replacing any retained file. A lost catalog commit reply recovers the accepted generation.",
    "The file inventory now covers publication journals, immutable recovery inputs, manual history, and scoped provider records under its existing private runtime policy."
  ],
  "format": {
    "publication_version": 2,
    "accepted_legacy_publication_version": 1,
    "manual_history_version": 1,
    "head": "R/catalog-runtime/manual.json",
    "inputs": "R/catalog-runtime/publication-inputs/<sha256>.json",
    "max_batches": 4096,
    "max_encoded_observation_bytes": 67108864,
    "native_upgrade_and_downgrade": "UNVERIFIED"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "CLI and HTTP acquisition still publish directly through the root client. Their runtime integration and transactional D24 reset scopes remain open.",
    "D24 preserves the embedded or selected upstream baseline while resetting selected local acquisition. The current pipeline still uses an empty baseline for sync.WithFresh and starmap update --force.",
    "Local projection provenance must prevent copied fields from restoring retired binding evidence. Field presence and scoped deletion remain open.",
    "History has fixed component limits and no compaction. CSP5 owns production compaction, collection, budgets, and operator recovery.",
    "These checks do not measure gateway request latency or allocations. Shared fleet recovery, authority enforcement, Starport adoption, and released-pair acceptance remain open.",
    "The full pre-publication repository gate, required code review, and native qualification remain open. No branch push, GitHub merge, release, or native CI dispatch occurred."
  ],
